This product is a TypeScript port of supernote-cloud
(https://github.com/rnbennett/supernote-cloud), maintained by Ryan Bennett,
which is a continuation of sncloud (https://github.com/julianprester/sncloud),
original work Copyright Julian Prester. Both are licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0.

Files ported from supernote-cloud carry a header naming the file they came
from. Changes made in the port:

- Rewritten from Python to TypeScript, with no runtime dependencies.
- The commands that change Supernote Cloud (put, mkdir, rename, mv, cp, rm)
  take their target as the last argument and refuse instead of overwriting:
  a taken name is an error, put --force replaces a file through a backup it
  can restore, rm asks first and needs -r for a folder with contents, mkdir
  gains -p, and items from different folders are handled one folder at a time.
- The access token is read from the SUPERNOTE_TOKEN environment variable and
  is never written to disk. `login` prints the token instead of saving it.
- File and folder ids are kept as strings, because they exceed the largest
  integer JavaScript numbers hold exactly.
- Folder listing follows every page instead of returning only the first 100
  items.
- Paths are resolved by matching each part by name, instead of guessing from
  a "." whether the last part is a file.
- Identity verification is signalled with an IdentityVerificationRequired
  error instead of an "__E1760__:<timestamp>" message string, and an expired
  or invalid token raises AccessTokenRejected.
- `get --pdf` and `get --png` also accept the .mark a device keeps beside a
  PDF: the cloud renders the PDF with its handwriting, and --png takes the
  handwriting back out of that rendering as transparent PNGs.

